{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 27, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "### Summary of the Wikipedia Page \"Raymond III Count of Tripoli\"\n\nRaymond III was Count of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187. He was the son of Raymond II of Tripoli and Hodierna of Rethel. Raymond III became count at a young age after his father was assassinated in 1152. His mother Hodierna acted as regent until he came of age. Raymond III was a key figure in the Crusader states during the 12th century.\n\n*highlighted section part 1*\nDuring his rule Raymond III faced challenges from the Muslim forces led by Nur ad-Din. In 1164 he was captured at the Battle of Harim and held prisoner for almost a decade until 1173. His absence left Tripoli vulnerable. Upon his release he resumed control and worked to strengthen the county. Raymond III also played a role in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem. He supported Amalric I and later Baldwin IV the leper king. Raymond III was married to Eschiva of Bures who brought the title Princess of Galilee to the marriage. Their union strengthened his influence in the region.\n\n*highlighted section part 2*\nRaymond III is best known for his role in the Battle of Hattin in 1187. He commanded a significant portion of the Crusader forces alongside Guy of Lusignan. The battle ended in a decisive Muslim victory under Saladin. Raymond III managed to escape but the defeat led to the fall of Jerusalem and much of the Crusader territories. He died shortly after in 1187 leaving Tripoli to his nephew Bohemond IV. His death marked the end of an era for the County of Tripoli and the Crusader states as a whole.\n\n*highlighted section part 3*\nRaymond III’s legacy is marked by his resilience and political acumen. Despite setbacks he maintained control over Tripoli and influenced the broader Crusader politics. His actions during Hattin and his earlier captivity shaped the fate of the Crusader states. Raymond III remains a notable figure in the history of the Latin East. His life reflects the struggles and challenges faced by the Crusaders during a turbulent period.", "logprobs": [{"token": "###", "logprob": -2.8484303951263428}, {"token": " Summary", "logprob": -1.070208191871643}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0023534002248197794}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.21017472445964813}, {"token": " Wikipedia", "logprob": -9.595887240720913e-05}, {"token": " Page", "logprob": -0.3486069440841675}, {"token": " \"", "logprob": -1.0060696601867676}, {"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.00016532962035853416}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -2.9802276912960224e-06}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -5.352353764465079e-05}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.0052820174023509026}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.504691630951129e-05}, {"token": " Tripoli", "logprob": -2.861018856492592e-06}, {"token": "\"\n\n", "logprob": -0.00025078488397412}, {"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.762336254119873}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -1.0728830375228426e-06}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -4.434487345861271e-05}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.38574767112731934}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.061965037137269974}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -5.960462772236497e-07}, {"token": " Tripoli", "logprob": -7.867782187531702e-06}, {"token": " from", "logprob": -0.0003033416287507862}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.0006889115320518613}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -1.6689160474925302e-05}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -9.893881360767409e-05}, {"token": "5", "logprob": -0.0005553610390052199}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -8.940297266235575e-05}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.34856873750686646}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.01253888476639986}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -5.602820692729438e-06}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -2.8013790142722428e-05}, {"token": "8", "logprob": -2.4914430468925275e-05}, {"token": "7", "logprob": -2.8609820219571702e-05}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.014290493912994862}, {"token": " He", "logprob": -0.0062771304